BlastEm on Fedora
=================

Run `blastem` without a ROM path to open the graphical game browser. User
configuration is stored in ~/.config/blastem/blastem.cfg; the packaged
configuration in /usr/share/blastem/default.cfg remains an immutable default.

This package contains no commercial game ROMs, Sega firmware, or BIOS images.
Users must supply legally obtained game software and any firmware they choose
to configure. The normal graphical interface and the default md1va3 model do
not need firmware.

The source tree also contains source code for an older ROM-based menu and a
small TMSS replacement ROM. Their generated binaries (menu.bin and tmss.md)
are not tracked upstream, and Fedora 44 does not provide the vasm cross
assembler needed to reproduce them. They are therefore intentionally omitted.
The built-in graphical interface replaces menu.bin. Models explicitly
configured with TMSS need a compatible ROM selected with the tmss_path setting.

The private terminal helper used by the native debugger is installed under
/usr/libexec/blastem. Packaged builds create its communication FIFOs inside a
random per-launch mode-0700 directory rather than at predictable /tmp names,
and launch the desktop's configured terminal through xdg-terminal-exec.
